  "slug": "metabolic-trait-robustness-microbial-e869",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and database updates from November 2026 pair LLM agents and enzyme foundation models with curated kinetic and stability records.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational access to enzyme function, where retrieval, prediction and curated data resources are developed in parallel. RIVER uses a multi-agent LLM framework with biochemical tools and validation modules to retrieve enzyme-reaction pairs bidirectionally. AlphaEnzyme is a structure-grounded enzyme foundation model that predicts catalyst retrieval, Km and mutational effects. On the data side, OrganiZymeDB curates 28,121 enzyme stability and function measurements in organic solvents from 646 publications, and the redesigned SABIO-RK adds a unified JSON curation framework, a 60+ field search and a RESTful API returning JSON, CSV, SBML or EnzymeML. What is new is the coupling of agentic and foundation-model retrieval to structured, machine-readable kinetic and stability records. The set is heterogeneous, so this thread is methodological rather than a demonstrated field-wide trend.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
